WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.200
AI can build a screen in minutes.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.500
Then, six weeks in, a store rule
says your checkout must change.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.900
Money, rules, what depends on
what: none of it was visible.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.500
I wish I'd known.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.600
Now you start over.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.600
Blueprint is a map of your
whole project, before you build.

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.400
Every decision sits in its column: brand,
screens, tech, money, rules, launch.

8
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.600
One look, and you see it all.

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.000
Tap a decision. You get the options, one
recommended pick, and the reason why.

10
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.300
Compare it with the
alternative we set aside.

11
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.400
See what else changes if you switch.

12
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.400
When it looks right, you approve it.

13
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.300
Add categories as your project grows.

14
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.100
Lines show real dependencies, so you
see what breaks before it breaks.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.400
Lessons from real projects return as
foresight: surprises others already hit.

16
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.700
AI proposes. Nothing is final
until a person says yes.

17
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.600
And AI coding tools like Claude Code,
Cursor and Codex read the same map,

18
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.400
through a local MCP
server or a YAML export.

19
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.600
See the whole project before you build.

20
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.400
Join the early prototype.

21
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.800
Creativity Is Everywhere, LLC.
